      "title": "Economic Activities Around Us",
      "explanation": "Economic activities are those that create monetary value and contribute to prosperity. They are classified into three sectors: Primary (directly from nature, e.g., agriculture, mining), Secondary (processing raw materials into goods, e.g., manufacturing furniture or cars), and Tertiary (providing services like banking, transportation, and healthcare). These sectors are interconnected, forming the foundation of economic life.",
